cl. 1. Ā. मोक्षते (rather Desid. fr. √ 2. मुच्; fut. मोक्षिष्यते, MBh.),
to wish to free one's self, seek deliverance, Kāṭh. (cf. Pāṇ. vii, 4, 57);
to free one's self from (acc.), shake off, MBh. ;
 cl. 10. P. (Dhātup. xxxiii, 57; rather Nom. fr. मोक्ष, below), मोक्षयति (mc. also Ā. ˚ते; Impv. मोक्षयध्वम्, MBh.; fut. मोक्षयिष्यति, ˚ते, ib.; inf. मोक्षितुम्, Hariv. v.l.),
to free or deliver from (abl.), Gaut.; Yājñ.; MBh. &c.;
to liberate, emancipate (from transmigration), Hariv.;
to loosen, untie, undo, Suśr.;
to detach, extract, draw out of (abl.), AitBr.;
to wrest or take away anything from (abl.), Hariv.;
to shed, cause to flow (blood), Suśr.;
to cast, hurl, fling, Dhātup.
